#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/db/structured_conditionals.rst:193
msgid ""
"Hum... Let's see... There's a set of AND's to join in. Let's start there."
msgstr ""
"Hmm... Lad os se... Der er et sæt AND'er at forbinde. Lad os starte der."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/db/structured_conditionals.rst:207
msgid "Inside the set of AND's, one of them is a set of OR's."
msgstr "Inde i sættet af AND'er er en af dem et sæt af OR'er."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/db/structured_conditionals.rst:223
msgid ""
"There! Better! But it still isn't that easy to work with. There's a string "
"for each comparison. BUT! If I use the type1 array mentioned above, I can "
"separate each one of those into a single thing! In this case..."
msgstr ""
"Sådan! Bedre! Men det er stadig ikke helt nemt at arbejde med. Der er en "
"streng for hver sammenligning. MEN! Hvis jeg bruger type1-arrayet nævnt "
"ovenfor, kan jeg opdele hver af dem i én ting! I dette tilfælde..."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/db/structured_conditionals.rst:238
msgid ""
"There you go! No variable interpolation, no explicit string concatenation, "
"in case of a requirement to build it or change it later, it becomes a very "
"straightforward task (see next section) and all data is properly escaped."
msgstr ""
"Sådan! Ingen variabelinterpolation, ingen eksplicit strengsammenkædning; "
"hvis det senere skal opbygges eller ændres, bliver det en meget ligetil "
"opgave (se næste afsnit), og alle data escapes korrekt."

